+## Code of Conduct
+
+This project and everyone participating in it is governed by the
+[Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md). By participating, you are expected to
+uphold this code. Report unacceptable behavior to
+[koosha@example.com](mailto:koosha@example.com).
+
+## Getting Started
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+- **Rust** ≥ 1.75 (see `rust-toolchain.toml`)
+- **mise** or **rustup** for toolchain management
+- **Task** (Taskfile runner) — `brew install go-task` or `mise use task`
+- **cargo-deny**, **cargo-audit**, **cargo-outdated** (optional but recommended)
+
+### Clone and Build
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/KooshaPari/Settly.git
+cd Settly
+cargo build
+cargo test
+```
+
+### Recommended Local Tasks
+
+```bash
+task quality       # fmt + lint + test + audit
+task quality:strict   # CI-equivalent pipeline
+```
+
+Or via `just`:
+
+```bash
+just check
+just ci
+```
+
+## Development Workflow
+
+1. **Fork** the repository (or work directly on a feature branch in the
+   upstream repo if you have write access).
+2. Create a feature branch following the convention `worktrees/<topic>/`:
+
+   ```bash
+   git checkout -b worktrees/your-feature-name
+   ```
+
+3. Make your changes in small, focused commits.
+4. Run the quality gate locally:
+
+   ```bash
+   task quality:strict
+   ```
+
+5. Push your branch and open a Pull Request against `main`.
+6. Address review feedback promptly.
+
+## Pull Request Process
+
+1. Update the `CHANGELOG.md` under the `## [Unreleased]` section for any
+   user-visible change.
+2. Ensure the PR description references any related issues.
+3. All CI checks must pass:
+   - Rust CI (`ci.yml`)
+   - Security audit (`security.yml`)
+   - cargo-deny (`cargo-deny.yml`)
+   - OpenSSF Scorecard (`scorecard.yml`)
+4. A CODEOWNER must approve before merge.
+5. Squash-merge with a conventional-commit-style message (see below).
+
+## Coding Standards
+
+- **Formatting**: `cargo fmt --all` (enforced in CI)
+- **Linting**: `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`
+- **Line length**: 100 chars (see `.editorconfig`)
+- **Indentation**: 4 spaces for Rust, 2 spaces for YAML/JSON/Markdown/TOML
+- **Documentation**: Public APIs must have rustdoc comments
+- **Error handling**: Use `thiserror` for library errors, `anyhow` only at
+  application boundaries
+- **No `unwrap()`/`expect()`** in library code without a justifying comment
+
+## Testing
+
+- **Unit tests** live alongside source in `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` blocks.
+- **Integration tests** live in `tests/` at the workspace root.
+- **Doctests** are encouraged for all public API examples.
+- **Coverage** is tracked via `cargo-llvm-cov` and reported via Codecov.
+
+Target: maintain or improve the line/branch coverage of touched modules.
+
+## Commit Messages
+
+We follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):
+
+```
+<type>(<scope>): <description>
+
+[optional body]
+
+[optional footer(s)]
+```
+
+Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`,
+`ci`, `chore`, `revert`.
+
+Examples:
+
+```
+feat(domain): add migration hooks for v2 schema
+fix(adapters): correct idempotency key collision
+docs: update README with migration guide
+ci: add OpenSSF scorecard workflow
+```
+
+## Reporting Bugs
+
+Use the [Bug Report](../../issues/new?template=bug.yml) issue template. Include:
+
+- A clear, descriptive title
+- Steps to reproduce
+- Expected vs. actual behavior
+- Rust version (`rustc --version`) and OS
+- Relevant logs or stack traces
+
+## Suggesting Features
+
+Use the [Feature Request](../../issues/new?template=feature.yml) template.
+Describe the motivation, proposed solution, and any alternatives considered.
+
+## License
+
+By contributing, you agree that your contributions will be dual-licensed under
+MIT OR Apache-2.0, at the discretion of the project maintainers. See
+[LICENSE](LICENSE) for details.
+
+## Questions?
+
+Open a discussion or reach out at [koosha@example.com](mailto:koosha@example.com).
