 # Security Policy
 
+## Supported Versions
+
+Settly is now maintained as a crate within the
+[Configra](https://github.com/KooshaPari/Configra) mono-repo. The versions of
+this standalone repo listed below are receiving security updates:
+
+| Version | Supported          |
+| ------- | ------------------ |
+| 0.1.x   | :white_check_mark: |
+| < 0.1   | :x:                |
+
 ## Reporting a Vulnerability
-If you discover a security vulnerability, please report it responsibly:
-1. Do not open a public GitHub issue.
-2. Email the maintainers.
-3. Allow time for assessment before public disclosure.
+
+**Please do not report security vulnerabilities through public GitHub issues.**
+
+Instead, please report them privately via one of the following channels:
+
+1. **Email**: [koosha@example.com](mailto:koosha@example.com) (encrypted
+   communication preferred — PGP key available on request).
+2. **GitHub Security Advisories**: Use the
+   [private vulnerability reporting](../../security/advisories/new) feature on
+   this repository.
+3. **Direct contact**: Reach out to a maintainer through a trusted channel.
+
+### What to Include
+
+To help us triage and respond quickly, please include as much of the following
+as possible:
+
+- **Type of vulnerability** (e.g., RCE, DoS, info disclosure, supply chain)
+- **Affected component(s)** and version(s)
+- **Attack scenario** and preconditions
+- **Proof-of-concept** or reproducer (private PoC strongly preferred)
+- **Impact assessment** (worst-case consequences)
+- **Your contact info** for follow-up questions
+
+### Our Commitments
+
+When you submit a report, we commit to:
+
+- **Acknowledge** receipt within **3 business days**
+- **Triage** and provide an initial assessment within **10 business days**
+- **Keep you informed** of progress toward a fix
+- **Credit** you in the advisory (unless you request anonymity)
+- **Coordinate disclosure** timing with you — we will not publicly disclose
+  the issue until a fix is available, or until an agreed-upon disclosure date
+
+### Safe Harbor
+
+We will not pursue legal action against researchers who:
+
+- Make a good-faith effort to avoid privacy violations, data destruction, or
+  service disruption
+- Only interact with accounts they own or have explicit permission to access
+- Stop testing immediately and report findings if they encounter user data
+- Do not exploit a vulnerability beyond what is necessary to demonstrate it
+
+## Security Update Process
+
+1. A private security advisory is opened.
+2. Maintainers triage, develop, and review a fix in a private fork.
+3. A release is prepared with the fix and a CVE is requested if applicable.
+4. Coordinated public disclosure occurs after a grace period (typically 90
+   days from confirmation, or sooner if a fix is available).
+5. The advisory is published with full credit to the reporter.
+
+## Supply Chain Security
+
+We employ the following supply-chain defenses:
+
+- **`cargo-deny`** (`deny.toml`) — enforces license allow-list, source
+  restrictions, and known-vulnerability checks
+- **`cargo-audit`** — runs on every CI run via the security workflow
+- **Dependabot** — weekly automated PRs for upstream advisories
+- **OpenSSF Scorecard** — periodic supply-chain posture evaluation
+- **Pinned GitHub Actions** via commit SHAs (where applicable)
+- **Branch protection** on `main` requiring CODEOWNER approval
+
+## Acknowledgments
+
+We gratefully acknowledge the security researchers and contributors who have
+helped improve Settly's security posture.
